\"filter\":\"raw\"}],\"time_distance\":\"2 hours\",\"content\":\"<p class=\\\"p1\\\">The Belly of the Dragon is quite the adventurous, scenic little hike. This carved tunnel hike passes under highway 89 and is used as a drainage for the upper canyons that feed into the North Fork River.<\\/p>\\n<p class=\\\"p1\\\">DO NOT enter the tunnel under any\\u00a0rainy conditions. There are a few spots of rock scrambling to get up and through the tunnel. There are carvings on the rock at the entrance to the tunnel. Please respect these walls and add no more &#8211; we wish to keep the natural beauty of this area Through the tunnel is a short hike. You may continue up the wash for about 4 miles, it ends at a beautiful little slot canyon.<\\/p>\\n<p class=\\\"p1\\\">There is amazing scenery around every bend. We are excited to have you come and explore our backyard with us.<\\/p>\\n\"},\"featured_image_url\":\"\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2021\\/01\\/DSC_6654-768x512.jpg\",\"_links\":{\"self\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/trail_maps\\/5935\"}],\"collection\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/trail_maps\"}],\"about\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/types\\/trail_maps\"}],\"author\":[{\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/users\\/8\"}],\"wp:featuredmedia\":[{\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/media\\/5937\"}],\"wp:attachment\":[{\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/media?parent=5935\"}],\"wp:term\":[{\"taxonomy\":\"difficulties\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/difficulties?post=5935\"},{\"taxonomy\":\"trail_types\",\"embeddable\":true,\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/visitsouthernutah.com\\/wp-json\\/wp\\/v2\\/trail_types?post=5935\"}],\"curies\":[{\"name\":\"wp\",\"href\":\"https:\\/\\/api.w.org\\/