the rim of the plateau to a more strenuous hike that descends down into the canyon along steep and rocky trails. More information will be given on the day of the event.<br \\/> <br \\/> <strong>2023 Schedule<\\/strong><\\/p> <ul> <li>January 4<\\/li> <li>February 4<\\/li> <li>March 7<\\/li> <li>No April Hike Scheduled<\\/li> <li>May 5<\\/li> <li>June 3<\\/li> <li>July 3<\\/li> <li>August 1<\\/li> <li>September 29<\\/li> <li>No October Hike Scheduled<\\/li> <li>November 27<\\/li> <li>December 26<\\/li> <\\/ul> <h4>Due to the nature of this special activity all participants must agree to the following rules:<\\/h4> <ul> <li>Children 7 and younger are not permitted.<\\/li> <li>Hiking boots or hiking shoes (lug soles) in good condition are required for your safety and the safety of Park Staff and other Participant(s).<\\/li> <li>White light flashlights, headlamps\\u00a0are not\\u00a0allowed to be used during the hike (you may bring them for later use). Red light flashlights and headlamps are permitted as necessary. Flash photography may be permitted under key restrictions.<\\/li> <li>Bring drinking water and a jacket - night time temperatures can be cold.<\\/li> <li>Due to steep and rocky trails this activity is not wheelchair accessible.<br \\/> \\u00a0<\\/li> <\\/ul>\",\"reservationDescription\":\"Reservations via lottery are required.<br \\/> <br \\/> Full Moon lotteries are held at 4 p.m. in the Visitor Center theater. All those hoping to join a Full Moon Hike must arrive at the Visitor Center a few minutes before 4 p.m. (Mountain Time) to be included in the lottery. Latecomers will not be allowed to participate.<br \\/> <br \\/> <strong>Each person in your group must be present at the lottery with the hiking shoes\\/boots they plan to wear.<\\/strong>\\u00a0Once your footwear has passed inspection, one lottery ticket will be issued per group.<br \\/> <br \\/> The Ranger giving you the lottery ticket will write the number in your party<strong>\\u00a0(maximum of 6)<\\/strong>\\u00a0on the back of your lottery ticket. If your lottery ticket is drawn, only the number of people written on the back of the winning lottery ticket will be issued hiker tickets.<br \\/> <br \\/> Contact us for more information about the lottery at brca_information@nps.gov.<br \\/> Hikes are canceled for cloudy skies or temperatures less than 10 degrees Farenheit (-12C).\",\"season\":[\"Winter\",\"Spring\",\"Summer\",\"Fall\"],\"topics\":[{\"id\":\"0D00073E-18C3-46E5-8727-2F87B112DDC6\",\"name\":\"Animals\"},{\"id\":\"BCE3ACBE-7871-495B-AEA3-5E19BC482405\",\"name\":\"Canyons and Canyonlands\"},{\"id\":\"4DC11D06-00F1-4A01-81D0-89CCCCE4FF50\",\"name\":\"Climate Change\"},{\"id\":\"A266302A-E2AE-4671-8515-B3614D8EF37F\",\"name\":\"Plateaus and Mesas\"},{\"id\":\"41B1A0A3-11FF-4F55-9CB9-034A7E28B087\",\"name\":\"Forests and Woodlands\"},{\"id\":\"F0F97E32-2F29-41B4-AF98-9FBE8DAB36B1\",\"name\":\"Geology\"},{\"id\":\"F8C2FE93-DEB3-4B12-9A87-913E3E6B448D\",\"name\":\"Natural Sounds\"},{\"id\":\"A7359FC4-DAD8-45F5-AF15-7FF62F816ED3\",\"name\":\"Night Sky\"},{\"id\":\"E06F3C94-AC8A-4B1C-A247-8EBA8910D5EE\",\"name\":\"Astronomy\"}],\"durationDescription\":\"\",\"arePetsPermitted\":\"false\",\"timeOfDay\":[\"Dusk\"],\"duration\":\"60-120 Minutes\",\"credit\":\"\"}',1,'2023-09-10 21:06:03','2023-09-10 21:06:32'),(338,'Bryce Canyon Evening Program','Bryce Canyon Lodge Auditorium','nps','A5182852-E474-4C11-97E6-6697978EFD71',1,'\\r\\n\\r\\n','Be sure to always check the Calendar or stop by the Visitor Center to find the programs that will be available during your visit.  Typically offered from Memorial Day through Labor Day in the auditorium of the historic Bryce Canyon Lodge at 8:30 p.m.  Evening programs offer topics that go beyond the rim!  Join a Ranger to explore the compelling stories, interesting themes, and unique resources that Bryce Canyon National Park protects. This is a Ranger’s Choice program.  Some of 2023 offerings include  “Finding Your Way – Introduction to Navigation” “Flower Power and the Effects of Nature on your Health and Wellbeing” “The Lighter Side of the Moon” “Thunder! Lightning! Very, Very Frightening” \"The Geology of the Grand Staircase\" Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark: Fire in Bryce Canyon\" “Have a Bryce Day!” “Adaptations in the Park”  A schedule of daily topics is available in the Visitor Center.',NULL,'This is a seated program and is accessible.','45-60 Minutes','1',37.6270245,-112.1679988,NULL,'https://www.nps.gov/thingstodo/bryce-canyon-evening-program.htm',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,NULL,'{\"id\":\"A5182852-E474-4C11-97E6-6697978EFD71\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/thingstodo\\/bryce-canyon-evening-program.htm\",\"title\":\"Bryce Canyon Evening Program\",\"shortDescription\":\"Typically offered from Memorial Day through Labor Day in the auditorium of the historic Bryce Canyon Lodge at 8:30 p.m. Evening programs offer topics that go beyond the rim! Join a Ranger to explore the compelling stories, interesting themes, and unique resources that Bryce Canyon National Park protects.\\u00a0This is a Ranger\\u2019s Choice program.\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/common\\/uploads\\/cropped_image\\/E5CCA03D-FDA1-4954-49ADDCEFFEA89CDC.jpg\",\"credit\":\"NPS Photo\",\"altText\":\"A ranger stands in front of a screen before a seated audience.\",\"title\":\"Bryce Canyon Evening Program\",\"description\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Bryce Canyon Evening Programs now take place in the Lodge Auditorium.\",\"crops\":[{\"aspectRatio\":\"1.78\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/common\\/uploads\\/cropped_image\\/primary\\/E5CCA03D-FDA1-4954-49ADDCEFFEA89CDC.jpg\"},{\"aspectRatio\":\"1\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.nps.gov\\/common\\/uploads\\/cropped_image\\/secondary\\/E5CCA03D-FDA1-4954-49ADDCEFFEA89CDC.jpg\"}]}],\"relatedParks\":[{\"states\":\"UT\",\"parkCode\":\"brca\",\"designation\":\"National Park\",\"fullName\":\"Bryce Canyon National P